#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:16
#: 217c98ac7a3645a2ae808ab4b8877e51
msgid "Lesson 1: Cloning Skeletons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:18
#: fb68cc027058476987a7671fe8082986
msgid ""
"There are often times where you might want to create an exact replica of "
"an existing Skeleton. DART offers cloning functionality that allows you "
"to do this very easily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:22
#: a8434484b86b40c184cccc32282d89ce
msgid "Lesson 1a: Create a new domino"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:24
#: aab489b256db44a48d5115ff8317378e
msgid ""
"Creating a new domino is straightforward. Find the "
"``DominoEventHandler::attemptToCreateDomino`` function. The event handler"
" keeps ``mFirstDomino`` as the original domino created when the program "
"starts up. To make a new one, we can just clone it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:33
#: 05b33a655e91491197d80b9d8b6c1932
msgid ""
"But keep in mind that every Skeleton that gets added to a world requires "
"its own unique name. Creating a clone will keep the original name, so we "
"should we give the new copy its own name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:41
#: 8a517cdb537c43aa8af2c4797fb7dcbf
msgid ""
"So the easy part is finished, but now we need to get the domino to the "
"correct position. First, let's grab the last domino that was placed in "
"the environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:49
#: 0586b8964b53411eb83b03722323935a
msgid ""
"Now we should compute what we want its position to be. The event handler "
"keeps a member called ``mTotalAngle`` which tracks how much the line of "
"dominoes has turned so far. We'll use that to figure out what "
"translational offset the new domino should have from the last domino:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:59
#: c6210dce7ad64a3aabf417acc4323aa3
msgid ""
"And now we can compute the total position of the new domino. First, we'll"
" copy the positions of the last domino:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:66
#: 3c039d2e86d34c8c836e7c371adff130
msgid "And then we'll add the translational offset to it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:72
#: e8f5d549f46a4e45b9d90cf94552c52c
msgid ""
"Remember that the domino's root joint is a FreeJoint which has six "
"degrees of freedom: the first three are for orientation and last three "
"are for translation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:75
#: 8b32ac3bf25c42dea6e1d7dd43bc99e3
msgid "Finally, we should add on the change in angle for the new domino:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:81
#: 605b6143b6d943e2833a9831192774e4
msgid "Be sure to uncomment the ``angle`` argument of the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:83
#: 3bc4e4a9ff414a778221fe57df49b403
msgid "Now we can use ``x`` to set the positions of the domino:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:89
#: 6e1e2f79aea44149b03786a1fb450e9a
msgid ""
"The root FreeJoint is the only joint in the domino's Skeleton, so we can "
"just use the ``Skeleton::setPositions`` function to set it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:92
#: bb52ed25a8054c4e9195e10c4280974e
msgid ""
"Before adding the Skeleton to the world, we'll check its placement for "
"collisions."
msgstr "Skeleton을 월드에 추가하기 전에 배치 위치에서 충돌이 발생하는지 확인합니다."

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:94
#: 1070427722254317a48befab0bf936de
msgid "Lesson 1b: Make sure no dominoes are in collision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:96
#: 9c90bd17f0b34a29b57ed7c9dd1c3dbe
msgid ""
"Similar to **Lesson 3** of the **Collisions** tutorial, we'll want to "
"make sure that the new Skeleton is not starting out in collision with "
"anything before adding it to the world. Check a collision group "
"containing only the new domino against the world's collision group:"
msgstr ""
"**Collisions** 튜토리얼의 **Lesson 3** 과 마찬가지로 새 Skeleton을 월드에 추가하기 전에 다른 물체와 "
"충돌하지 않는지 확인해야 합니다. 새 도미노만 포함하는 충돌 그룹을 월드의 충돌 그룹과 비교하세요:"

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:108
#: 162e76a861bd42d2a0c4e2e87c2defbb
msgid ""
"The domino should rest on the floor, so temporarily exclude the floor's "
"shape frames from the world's collision group. Restore them immediately "
"after the check so that the floor still participates in the simulation:"
msgstr ""
"도미노는 바닥 위에 놓여야 하므로, 월드의 충돌 그룹에서 바닥의 ShapeFrame을 잠시 제외합니다. 검사 직후 다시 추가하여 "
"바닥이 계속 시뮬레이션에 참여하도록 하세요:"

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:118
#: 5a022d7a2f7949959b6a92e87c60e7d8
msgid ""
"If the new domino is collision-free, add it to the world and record it in"
" the history. Otherwise, leave it out and explain how to try another "
"placement:"
msgstr "새 도미노가 충돌하지 않으면 월드에 추가하고 이력에 기록합니다. 충돌한다면 추가하지 않고 다른 배치를 시도하는 방법을 안내합니다:"

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:138
#: 0112e32f8cce41d183ff941911232602
msgid "Lesson 1c: Delete the last domino added"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:140
#: b36f3684e47040349a083d701857894c
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, removing a Skeleton from a scene is just a matter of calling "
"the ``World::removeSkeleton`` function, but we have a little bit of "
"bookkeeping to take care of for our particular application. First, we "
"should check whether there are any dominoes to actually remove:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:152
#: 1292bf64f67b44cfa58dff64dd08f471
msgid ""
"Then we should grab the last domino in the history, remove it from the "
"history, and then take it out of the world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:161
#: de62ef8365a44541ab34804f5c763164
msgid ""
"The ``SkeletonPtr`` class is really a ``std::shared_ptr<Skeleton>`` so we"
" don't need to worry about ever calling ``delete`` on it. Instead, its "
"resources will be freed when ``lastDomino`` goes out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:165
#: 340966a39fcf4ba09dd8efe740ebe65f
msgid "We should also make sure to do the bookkeepping for the angles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:172
#: 4610619249684e3892f47c50d9d1dc9d
msgid ""
"**Now we can add and remove dominoes from the scene. Feel free to give it"
" a try.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:174
#: d552067b088241e79b9b20ae21fb5275
msgid "Lesson 1d: Apply a force to the first domino"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dart/user_guide/tutorials/dominoes.md:176
#: 34cf324cc59a44fca20744e91c8a16c9
msgid ""
"But just setting up dominoes isn't much fun without being able to knock "
"them down. We can quickly and easily knock down the dominoes by magically"
" applying a force to the first one. Inside "
